    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bccebe36"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Summary of EDA and Feature Engineering Insights\n",
        "\n",
        "- The dataset contains **2850 unique customer records** and **14 features**, including the target variable 'Churn'.\n",
        "- There are **no missing values**.\n",
        "- The target variable, 'Churn', is **imbalanced**, with a lower number of churned customers (15.65%). This suggests the need for techniques to handle class imbalance during model training, if necessary.\n",
        "- **Numerical features** like 'Seconds of Use', 'Frequency of use', 'Frequency of SMS', 'Distinct Called Numbers', and 'Customer Value' show varying distributions, some skewed, which might benefit from transformation or scaling.\n",
        "- **Categorical features** such as 'Complains', 'Age Group', 'Tariff Plan', and 'Status' exhibit distinct patterns when cross-referenced with 'Churn', indicating their potential importance as predictors.\n",
        "  - 'Complains': Customers who complain ('Complains' = 1) show a significantly higher churn rate.\n",
        "  - 'Tariff Plan' and 'Status' also show some distribution differences between churned and non-churned customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on these insights, we will now proceed with preparing the data for modeling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "897c21d2"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Split the Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "Before training a model, we need to split the data into features (X) and the target variable (y). We will also handle categorical features by applying one-hot encoding, and then split the dataset into training and testing sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3b3da735",
        "outputId": "a9a19080-37f0-4789-a6c7-429f1e6cec60"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Separate target variable\n",
        "X = df.drop('Churn', axis=1)\n",
        "y = df['Churn']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Identify categorical columns for one-hot encoding\n",
        "# Exclude 'Complains' from here as it's already binary (0/1)\n",
        "# 'Age Group', 'Tariff Plan', 'Status' are encoded as integers but are categorical\n",
        "categorical_features_to_encode = ['Age Group', 'Tariff Plan', 'Status']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply one-hot encoding to specified categorical features\n",
        "X = pd.get_dummies(X, columns=categorical_features_to_encode, drop_first=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Shape of X after one-hot encoding:', X.shape)\n",
        "print('First 5 rows of X after encoding:')\n",
        "print(X.head())"
      ],
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
