      "source": [
        "## 5. Choose the Classification Algorithm\n",
        "\n",
        "Since 'Churn' is a binary outcome (0 or 1), this is a classification problem rather than a regression problem. We will start with Logistic Regression, a commonly used algorithm for binary classification, as our initial model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "eb5f704e",
        "outputId": "5c328cf1-391b-4e61-eb1e-e45546ac9bd6"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize the Logistic Regression model\n",
        "model = LogisticRegression(random_state=42, solver='liblinear')\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Logistic Regression model initialized.')"
      ],
      "execution_count": 23,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
